<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Ask</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre> ask &lt;character&gt; (sentence asking for something?)
 ask (sentence asking for something?)
</pre>
<p>Ask is mostly same as say, except this is directed as a character
question: "Gnort asks you '...'". Everyone in the room hears the
question, just as with say. If the first word isn't someone in the room,
you ask the room at large. To keep a question between the two of you,
whisper it instead.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre> <a cmd='#'>Help Tell</a>
 <a cmd='#'>Help Shout</a>
 <a cmd='#'>Help Say</a>
 <a cmd='#'>Help Whisper</a>
</pre>




</div>